## Tutorials

❮ Math Methods

Theabs()method returns the absolute (positive) value of a number.

One of the following:

### Code Examples

```
Example
Return the absolute (positive) value of different numbers:
System.out.println(Math.abs(-4.7));
System.out.println(Math.abs(4.7));
System.out.println(Math.abs(3));
Try it Yourself »
```

## Tutorials

❮ Math Methods

Theacos()method returns the arc cosine 
value of a number.

Tip:acos(-1) returns the value of PI.

### Code Examples

```
Example
Return the arc cosine of different numbers:
System.out.println(Math.acos(0.64));
System.out.println(Math.acos(-0.4));
System.out.println(Math.acos(0));
System.out.println(Math.acos(1));
System.out.println(Math.acos(-1));
System.out.println(Math.acos(2));
Try it Yourself »
```

